id: pm-brief-action-prerequisites
title: Compose a compact prerequisite brief for one intended native action
description: "Combine SDK command contracts, item readiness and declared evidence for an explicitly selected native command and item. Compose authoritative core facts without duplicating validators or selecting work."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-27T04:25:34.000Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-27T09:24:26.249Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "One call identifies missing close fields and unresolved prerequisites; Satisfied fields are references without repeated bodies; Read-only previews perform zero mutations and carry typed unsupported-capability refusals with remedies; Typed SDK and CLI emit bounded TOON/JSON; docs, non-git public-data validation and npm/Bun release evidence are recorded"
comments[21]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-27T04:25:48.456Z",codex-agent,"Overlap rechecked against pinned SDK public contracts/actionability/lifecycle/schema declarations, core command discovery, pm-lint quality rules and pm-evidence selectors, plus existing tracker items and upstream issue search. Core owns native command availability, lifecycle admission and configured status semantics; pm-lint owns quality diagnosis; pm-evidence owns evidence collection. This feature composes those facts for one explicit action and item, without selecting work, applying actions or creating a second validator. No existing action prerequisite item or GitHub issue found. Plan: typed bounded preview, native command registration, strict shared request schema, reference-only satisfied evidence, non-git and no-write regressions, public-copy measurement, packed install matrix and CI npm/Bun gates. Import/export/sync and journal mutation paths are outside this read-only feature; existing paths remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-27T04:31:37.604Z",codex-agent,"Implementation now composes getContracts availability, certified complete-list reads, resolveItemBlockers (including reverse/external/missing edges), runtime status roles, computeActionabilityReport, native transition evaluation, workflow policy evaluation and SDK lifecycle completeness presets. Satisfied evidence is item/input JSON Pointer references, never copied bodies. Validation found that cold native certified reads initialize derived runtime metadata caches; item/schema/history bytes remain unchanged. Warm repeated previews also preserve all runtime bytes. This distinction will be explicit in measured evidence rather than claiming the SDK performs no derived cache IO."
  "2026-10-27T04:41:28.338Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: replacing only buildActionPrerequisiteBrief with a no-op empty ready preview makes the combined prerequisite regression fail with exit 1; restoring the implementation passes that exact regression with exit 0. Focused suite passed 9/9 including 500 seeded random sequences on a native non-git tracker; parser/output numeric checks, native status roles, old-request replays, SDK read-back state and native competing writes are exercised. Public origin/main snapshot 04b258644a746d289455d1287dd84b5bafe6aa1a: 98 certified items/previews, 115 missing inputs, 277 satisfied references, 0 unresolved references in this corpus, 1486 maximum JSON bytes, 808 maximum conservative tokens, 97601ms elapsed, 0 tracker byte changes under physical read-only permissions. Details and source fingerprint are in docs/action-validation.md. Rechecked SDK staged mutation preview APIs as well: they execute disposable mutations and do not expose a read-only aggregate of missing action inputs; this composition uses public fact/policy readers instead."
  "2026-10-27T04:43:21.456Z",codex-agent,"Local TypeScript source/tests and docstring lint pass (15 files, 183 documented declarations); diff whitespace is clean. Native command argument metadata and singleton read-output declaration are registered. The mandatory linked combined regression is kept targeted for the saturated host; a broader linked attempt reached its default 120-second timeout, while the independent 500-sequence focused suite passed with a longer explicit allowance. Full release and packed matrix evidence will come from CI, with unchanged coverage thresholds. Bun global isolation was smoke-verified using disposable global directory/bin environment coordinates; no executable or SDK is located via argv/which/symlink heuristics."
  "2026-10-27T04:44:45.002Z",codex-agent,"PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-brief/pull/189 is ready for review. Current deterministic action/renderer checks pass 9/9, with new action.ts measured at 100% lines, 99.07% branches and 100% functions; the pm-linked combined regression passes 1/1. Source/test typechecks, docstring lint and changelog check pass. Full npm and Bun release gates are queued at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-brief/actions/runs/40451376112 on commit 62bb8f1bf9a07a852d9e856276e2e42195412c3e; final counts will be reported on the PR after the final head passes. No item is closed, merged or released to a registry."
  "2026-10-27T04:52:44.050Z",codex-agent,"Packed acceptance now resolves the current stable public CLI version for both disposable global scenarios, while project-local npm/Bun cases retain the repository development pin and the minimum-host case retains the declared peer floor. This verifies the current global host without a dependency bump. The earlier queued CI head is superseded only for this validation correction; no native action implementation changed."
  "2026-10-27T05:17:28.827Z",codex-agent,"Self-review found and fixed action scoping: work-dispatch human/gate/active-status classifications must not block an otherwise evidenced close. A new native non-git regression fails against the unconditional readiness checks and passes with action-specific checks for Decision, Milestone, blocked and draft items. Close prerequisites now use the SDK buildItemChildrenRollup and expose unfinished direct-child ids as references; terminal done/canceled children do not gate closure. The helper and all used policy/complete-list APIs were also verified in the public SDK surface of the declared minimum host 2026.10.13. The previous head 9f9635a passed both npm and Bun release gates with 616 tests and five packed scenarios, including global CLI 2026.10.26; those results are preliminary and the corrected final head will receive fresh complete gates."
  "2026-10-27T05:21:32.372Z",codex-agent,"Corrected final local evidence: 10/10 deterministic action/renderer tests pass; action.ts coverage is 100% lines, 98.69% branches and 100% functions. Both pm-linked regressions pass 2/2. Source/test TypeScript checks and docstring lint pass. The repeated physically read-only public-copy measurement preserves the same fingerprint and counts (98 previews, 115 missing inputs, 277 satisfied references, maximum 1486 JSON bytes / 808 conservative tokens, zero changed bytes); updated elapsed time is 166174ms on the shared host. Full CI 40452258248 passed all five jobs on the preceding head, but fresh exact-head npm/Bun and compatibility gates are required for this action-scoping correction and will be reported on the PR. Implementation and measurement files are linked on this item; it remains nonterminal for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-27T05:55:01.790Z",codex-agent,"A real native-policy reproduction exposed another unsafe projection: closing clears assignment, so a field-writer or field-requirement policy on assignee can be refused by native close even when a scalar-only proposed record appears satisfied. The regression fails against the earlier implementation. Matching workspace field/writer policies now carry unsupported-capability refusals with a native semantic-preview remedy; approval-history refusals remain explicit. Start-task also refuses matching claim-stage policies rather than silently checking only its update stage. Native start-status and author resolution now use the public SDK helpers. These are read-only capability boundaries, not replacement validators or staged mutations."
  "2026-10-27T06:05:38.756Z",codex-agent,"The native policy regression now also proves strict ownership on close: another principal is unresolved, an undeclared actor is a missing input, and the matching normalized actor passes. Ownership comparison uses the SDK claim-principal resolver, while the SDK start-task status resolver handles lifecycle selection. Current policy-focused checks pass against native close/start refusals; the public tracker uses ownership mode none and has no matching workspace field/claim policies, so its recorded read-only checklist counts remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-27T06:10:15.089Z",codex-agent,"Final targeted evidence after the policy/principal correction: 11/11 deterministic action/renderer tests pass with action.ts at 100% lines, 97.95% branches and 100% functions; all three pm-linked native regressions pass 3/3. Source/test TypeScript and docstring checks pass. Packed acceptance now includes seven distinct consumers: pinned npm/Bun project-local installs, the minimum host, current npm/Bun global hosts, and current npx/bunx ephemeral hosts with no project-local host. This distinguishes acquisition from merely invoking a local bin through a runner. The current published global/ephemeral host is resolved from the registry without changing development pins. Fresh exact-head gates will be reported on PR 189."
  "2026-10-27T06:34:13.841Z",codex-agent,"An adversarial input regression exposed a density hole: inherited array entries plus unrelated own keys could satisfy a key-count-only check. The shared request parser now snapshots bounded own data descriptors, rejects proxies/accessors, and validates each own array index without invoking iterators or getters. The regression fails against the previous parser and includes revoked proxies and non-executed accessor assertions. This preserves one JSON-data boundary for CLI and SDK callers, including producer round trips; no tracker or native action is touched during validation."
  "2026-10-27T06:37:02.016Z",codex-agent,"Final input-boundary verification passes: 11/11 deterministic native action and renderer checks; new source coverage 100% lines, 98.05% branches, 100% functions. Source and test TypeScript builds, typecheck and docstring lint pass (15 files, 184 declarations). All four pm-linked regressions pass 4/4 with no skipped executions. The preceding implementation head also passed CI run 40459755736: npm and Bun release gates each passed 618 tests with zero failures/skips, and all seven packed consumer scenarios including the newly published current host 2026.10.27. The input-boundary commit will receive fresh exact-head gates, with final run counts linked on PR 189; the item remains in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-27T07:29:09.815Z",codex-agent,"Re-review round 1 identifies three admission-class defects: composed start-task admission must include type command-option policies; historical claim principal metadata is not a live claim without an assignee; and dispatch selection classifications must not deny an explicitly selected native action. The branch is current with origin/main (zero commits behind); no merge is required. Public PR threads and the supplied round-1 review contain no additional non-blocking findings. Plan: audit all package admission/ownership paths and consumers, reproduce each defect on native non-git trackers, compose public SDK policy helpers, add native execution agreement/property regressions plus SDK/CLI JSON/TOON and packed-install coverage, prove each behavioral revert, then run exact-head CI npm/Bun gates at unchanged thresholds. Existing dispatch-classification coverage will remain while its false action-admission expectation is replaced by stronger native-execution agreement."
  "2026-10-27T07:40:37.940Z",codex-agent,"Class audit completed across all runtime sources, SDK entry points, native registration/rendering and installed consumers. Rule 1: composed actions must account for every constituent command and distinguish invocation-option presence from persisted fields; start now uses resolveTypeDefinition, resolveCommandOptionPolicyState and commandOptionFlagLabel for required/disabled/hidden/error states, while close does not inherit update policies. Arbitrary required start flags are explicit missing entries plus unsupported refusals/remedies because the request does not accept those mutation options. Rule 2: ownership admission requires a current nonblank assignee; residual principals after native close/reopen no longer block either start or strict close, while legacy assignee-only claims still deny other actors. Rule 3: dispatch selection roles and nonterminal classifications are not explicit action admission; human/gate/container/blocked/draft classifications no longer veto selected starts, and native terminal/relationship checks remain. Other assignee uses are display/filter/history paths in index.ts and disclosure.ts, not competing admission implementations. All consumers share action.ts; JSON/TOON native non-git and all seven packed npm/Bun scenarios now exercise these classes. The existing classification test still verifies SDK container/human/gate/blocked facts and now also verifies successful native execution, so coverage was strengthened rather than removed."
  "2026-10-27T07:45:31.281Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof for each review class: kept all expanded tests unchanged and replaced only buildActionPrerequisiteBrief with its previous committed implementation, restoring only its original SDK import dependency. The composed-option regression failed because description was reported ready despite the required invocation flag; the ownership regression failed on a replayed close/reopen record with no assignee and a residual principal; the dispatch regression failed on an explicitly selected nonterminal container/human/gate case. Control result: 0 passed, 3 assertion failures, exit 1. The fixed source was restored byte-for-byte. Before the control, the complete deterministic action/renderer selection passed 14/14, with action.ts at 100% lines, 98.53% branches, 100% functions; source/test typechecks and docstring lint passed. No existing test was deleted, skipped or relaxed; SDK classification assertions remain and native action agreement was added. The prior physical read-only public-close measurement is retained: this revision changes start admission and strict ownership, while that corpus uses ownership mode none and no matching type policies."
  "2026-10-27T07:48:58.536Z",codex-agent,"Restored implementation passes all seven linked regressions (7/7, zero skipped or failed); result tracking is disabled by the existing project policy, so this comment records the receipt without changing that policy. Focused action/renderer tests pass 14/14, source/test typechecks and docstring lint pass, and action.ts coverage is 100% lines / 98.53% branches / 100% functions. The declared minimum host public SDK includes all new type-policy resolver/flag-label signatures. Expanded packed receipts will separately certify required invocation options, live ownership and explicit starts across npm/Bun local/global/ephemeral consumers. The three supplied blocking findings are fixed as classes; no other non-blocking review finding was supplied or found in public threads. Exact-head npm/Bun full gates and measured counts will be reported on PR 189. The item stays in progress for orchestrator verification; no upstream CLI issue or SDK gap was identified."
  "2026-10-27T08:32:04.935Z",codex-agent,"Round-2 re-review identifies a severity-class defect: advisory findings and warning-only workflow transitions must remain visible without becoming required prerequisites. The worktree is clean and current with origin/main, so no merge is needed. The supplied review and public threads contain no additional non-blocking finding. Audit scope includes every workspace policy kind, global enforcement mode, explicit rule effect, composed claim/update stages, close, unknown actors, transition modes, SDK/CLI JSON/TOON and all packed consumers. Native SDK decision severity will determine gating; explicit requested evidence and intrinsic close inputs remain required. Tests will compare native execution and must-refuse controls, keep all existing assertions, and prove behavioral failure with only the changed builder reverted."
  "2026-10-27T09:14:50.807Z",codex-agent,"Round-2 class audit completed: every workspace policy kind now uses the SDK effective effect after registry enforcement, including claim-stage constraints, unknown actors and uncertified generated-field/approval checks. Advisory entries retain missing/unresolved facts with blocking:false; only effective refusals create mandatory policy gates or unsupported-capability refusals. SDK source inspection also established that type workflows govern the native start update, not direct close, and that close field/child validation is controlled by close_validation_default. The implementation follows those modes instead of treating all completeness advice as mandatory; explicit required evidence and native required reasons remain mandatory. The 120-case native matrix covers five rule kinds, two registry modes, four declared effects and three stages, with body-bearing SDK read-back and native must-allow/must-refuse controls. A first growing-corpus fixture timed out on the shared host; all cases/assertions were preserved while reusing one SDK-reset target to avoid quadratic tracker scans, and the matrix passed 120 cases. The test allowance accommodates shared-host variance. The remaining focused selection passes 15/15 with action.ts at 100% lines, 98.31% branches and 100% functions. Behavioral revert: restoring only the prior builder and its original SDK import yields 0 passed / 2 assertion failures, one advisory-policy failure and one warning-transition failure; fixed source restored byte-for-byte. No existing assertion was removed; the blocking approval fixture now explicitly declares refusing enforcement to retain its original refusal assertion."
  "2026-10-27T09:15:05.800Z",codex-agent,"Fresh physical read-only public replay independently verified all 203 source files against the public main snapshot. Results: 98 previews, 115 missing input facts (mandatory and advisory), 277 satisfied references, 0 unresolved prerequisite references or capability refusals in this corpus, 1639 maximum JSON bytes, 884 maximum conservative tokens, 68546ms elapsed and zero changed tracker bytes. Source fingerprint remains 835e5ee38de52a797bd5cc804b9a3767660add1446ef2ef90d4cfbc021fff891. Observed pinned-SDK diagnostic limitation: ClaimResult.warnings exposes takeover diagnostics but runClaim does not forward generic policy warnings; SDK evaluation still returns those diagnostics, and this preview uses that evaluator directly. The public declaration was inspected and the upstream issue search found no matching report; no issue was filed and this does not leave an acceptance criterion unmet."
  "2026-10-27T09:24:20.640Z",codex-agent,"Final round-2 local receipt: all nine linked checks pass 9/9 with zero failed or skipped executions after the behavioral revert was restored. The exhaustive severity matrix retains all 120 native cases; 15 other focused native/renderer checks pass, including non-git JSON/TOON and injected-context agreement. Source/test TypeScript checks and docstring lint pass (15 files, 184 declarations); focused action.ts coverage is 100% lines / 98.31% branches / 100% functions. Minimum-host public declarations include WorkflowPolicyEffect. Every changed runtime/test/doc path is already linked on this item. The blocking round-2 finding is addressed across all policy kinds/stages and native enforcement modes; no additional non-blocking finding was supplied or found. Fresh exact-head npm/Bun release gates will be linked and reported on PR 189, with no dependency pin or threshold change. Existing project test-result tracking remains disabled; this comment records the verified receipt without changing that policy. The item stays in progress for orchestrator verification."
